\]

**Step 2: Compute the hospital’s cost (what it pays doctors)**  

Doctors charge the hospital \$142 per hour.

\[
\text{Cost}=142 \times \frac{1015}{3}
           =\frac{142 \times 1015}{3}
           =\frac{144130}{3}
           =48\,043\frac13\text{ dollars}
\]

**Step 3: Compute the hospital’s revenue (what it charges patients)**  

The hospital charges patients \$409 per hour.

\[
\text{Revenue}=409 \times \frac{1015}{3}
               =\frac{409 \times 1015}{3}
               =\frac{415135}{3}
               =138\,378\frac13\text{ dollars}
\]

**Step 4: Compute profit**  

\[
\text{Profit}= \text{Revenue} - \text{Cost}
             =\frac{415135}{3} - \frac{144130}{3}
             =\frac{415135-144130}{3}
             =\frac{271005}{3}
             =90\,335\text{ dollars}
\]

The hospital earns **90 335** dollars profit from these daily visits.

